{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1533114-electric-lunar","id":1533114,"title":"Electric Lunar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-25T04:01:55-07:00","id":1533114,"title":"Electric Lunar","content":"What mutations do you think could be used to simulate electroreception and electrogenesis?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T08:01:27-07:00","id":1533124,"title":"","content":"Why stop at mutations? Seems like you could go back and grab the concept from the Alchemicals and modify it for use in water as a shapeshifting effect for their Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T03:49:03-07:00","id":1533160,"title":"","content":"Well, I just wanted to make an electric ray hybrid shape, I didn't think that far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T07:17:32-07:00","id":1533168,"title":"","content":"2e had the &quot;shark sight&quot; affliction (CotD: West), but it seemed to want to disavow having anything to do with modern physics and mentioned &quot;internal Essences&quot; as being what was picked up. I'd advise not doing that, but it's your game (if you go with the real life way, you won't have to re-invent wacky magic physiology that reproduces exactly what exists in real life, and you can have characters that can feel heartbeat pulses). At any rate, it was fairly abstract and non-mechanical in its workings, so it'd just allow for detection of others as normal in the ranges given, unless there was some kind of interference.<br /> <br /> A mutation for shocking was probably something under the envelope of the dragon's breath abomination in past editions. I'm not sure if it's still in EX3. I could see it being restricted to working at full in water only, but some eels in the OG oceanic book for 1e, Savage Seas, could straight up fire lightning bolts at their targets, so who knows what the setting of Exalted finds preferable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T15:23:01-07:00","id":1533212,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, I can't think of any merits (mutation or not) in 3rd edition that work directly like that. <br /> Except now, I'm wondering if a re-flavoured echolocation might work for electroreception. But now I am questioning if I am remembering that being available in 3e is correct.<br /> <br /> Electrogenesis feels like something that could be a shape-based charm actually. I know there are lunar charms that let you take eclipse charms based on your spirit shape and this could be one of those even if you have a hybrid spirit shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T15:27:01-07:00","id":1533213,"title":"","content":"Ah, the continued failure of the books to give Lunars the ability to shock people for 22 years. My recurring nemesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T10:00:13-07:00","id":1533517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1533114-electric-lunar?p=1533168#post1533168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some eels in the OG oceanic book for 1e, Savage Seas, could straight up fire lightning bolts at their targets, so who knows what the setting of Exalted finds preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that thus far Third Edition has maintained a decent standard of keeping its mundane animals within realms of plausibility at the same time that it includes more overtly magical creatures. I think something that shoots lightning bolts could exist, but would be under the same header as Fogsharks.<br /> <br /> As I recall, Dragon's Breath was something that existed kind of awkwardly alongside Natural Weapon in the first place, with the boundaries between the two never really hashed out beyond assuming the former to be all around superior. It being an Abomination also being a function of the messy way the game chose to implement being mutated by Wyld and similar folded into being granted extra powers by it.<br /> <br /> With that being said, while I think Third Edition Supernatural Merits have done a decent job of remaining relatively grounded thus far, I think delivering an bioelectrical shock could function as a reasonable option for expressing the Natural Weapon Merit, including its options for greater range and inflicting lethal damage. I think if a person was not going to be satisfied with that, they'd need to offer an idea of what they'd want for shocking that would be distinct from it.<br /> <br /> To answer another question, echolocation is available as both a Supernatural Merit and an innate Merit for the likes of bats and dolphins (the animal one working slightly differently and being a little better).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T10:15:22-07:00","id":1533518,"title":"","content":"As for myself, I think electroreception would make the most sense as providing a modifier for tracking actions; I think the stakes for those might be low enough that something fancy like doubling 9s would be permissible, unless one wanted to go for it providing a specific bonus for detecting targets that are concealed in some fashion. I'd say that as a Supernatural Merit, it would make sense to have a cheap version that only works in (sea) water and a more expensive one that can feel through the air, as well as modifiers for range. <br /> <br /> I'm a bit unsure about a Lunar Charm with a Protean effect to key off of it, as it's my opinion that electroreception is a bit less iconic than echolocation to be the basis for a Lunar Charm all on its own, and I think their capabilities are sophisticated enough now that it's not necessary to try and model every noteworthy animal capability as its own Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T10:21:39-07:00","id":1533519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1533114-electric-lunar?p=1533518#post1533518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for myself, I think electroreception would make the most sense as providing a modifier for tracking actions; I think the stakes for those might be low enough that something fancy like doubling 9s would be permissible, unless one wanted to go for it providing a specific bonus for detecting targets that are concealed in some fashion. I'd say that as a Supernatural Merit, it would make sense to have a cheap version that only works in (sea) water and a more expensive one that can feel through the air, as well as modifiers for range.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit unsure about a Lunar Charm with a Protean effect to key off of it, as it's my opinion that electroreception is a bit less iconic than echolocation to be the basis for a Lunar Charm all on its own, and I think their capabilities are sophisticated enough now that it's not necessary to try and model every noteworthy animal capability as its own Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the principle niche-spaces that it allows is detecting prey that are completely concealed to vision. It's how hammerhead sharks find stingrays that have buried themselves under the sand. It seems like it would allow for a chance to perceive others where no effect was normally possible to someone relying on other senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T16:35:16-07:00","id":1533541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1533114-electric-lunar?p=1533519#post1533519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the principle niche-spaces that it allows is detecting prey that are completely concealed to vision. It's how hammerhead sharks find stingrays that have buried themselves under the sand. It seems like it would allow for a chance to perceive others where no effect was normally possible to someone relying on other senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that becomes a bit of an air-breathing mermaid when Lunars already have a bunch of Perception Charms for enhancement to detecting targets in concealment that are pretty agnostic about which senses in particular are used to do so.<br /> <br /> Or else something calibrated for an extremely niche situation where a Storyteller deems a target to be concealed in a fashion that is completely imperceptible to all other senses, and even then going for an avenue of &quot;gain a new sense exclusively for this situation&quot; rather than &quot;sense becomes enhanced to mythic extent&quot;.<br /> <br /> At most, I think it could be something incorporated into a Charm with a range of options for the aesthetic of a Lunar's sensory enhancement to deal with something like penalties due to concealment that particularly obscures, similar to how there are Charms for things like making ammo or gliding that provide a bit of freedom for how exactly that manifests.<br /> <br /> Also keeping in mind that the system is biased more towards doing something with difficulty than being prevented from doing anything at all. A character who has no sense of vision is given a -3 penalty to perform actions that are primarily reliant on sight. I don't think there's organically a level of concealment that cuts off other methods of detection completely (barring the use of supernatural power), because otherwise, well, it makes a character somewhat helpless if they don't have electroreception, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T17:14:33-07:00","id":1533544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1533114-electric-lunar?p=1533541#post1533541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that becomes a bit of an air-breathing mermaid when Lunars already have a bunch of Perception Charms for enhancement to detecting targets in concealment that are pretty agnostic about which senses in particular are used to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the Silver Solars ride again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or else something calibrated for an extremely niche situation where a Storyteller deems a target to be concealed in a fashion that is completely imperceptible to all other senses, and even then going for an avenue of &quot;gain a new sense exclusively for this situation&quot; rather than &quot;sense becomes enhanced to mythic extent&quot;.<br /> <br /> At most, I think it could be something incorporated into a Charm with a range of options for the aesthetic of a Lunar's sensory enhancement to deal with something like penalties due to concealment that particularly obscures, similar to how there are Charms for things like making ammo or gliding that provide a bit of freedom for how exactly that manifests.<br /> <br /> Also keeping in mind that the system is biased more towards doing something with difficulty than being prevented from doing anything at all. A character who has no sense of vision is given a -3 penalty to perform actions that are primarily reliant on sight. I don't think there's organically a level of concealment that cuts off other methods of detection completely (barring the use of supernatural power), because otherwise, well, it makes a character somewhat helpless if they don't have electroreception, doesn't it? </div> </div> </div>In that case it would probably work in a break point so that it becomes &quot;detect before you get shanked&quot; rather than just &quot;detect&quot;. Not that it seems to matter with how indistinct and unstriking the Charms are by your description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T18:27:52-07:00","id":1533547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1533114-electric-lunar?p=1533544#post1533544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like the Silver Solars ride again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am unmoved by these buzzwords. The Third Edition Lunar Charm set managed to create something with an evocative character that has been generally well-received as a presentation of the personality depicted in the setting fiction and meaningfully distinct from other Exalted without going the route of body modification for the sake of every response or generally trying to bring in every halfway cool animal ability.<br /> <br /> I would propose an approach that is consistent with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that it seems to matter with how indistinct and unstriking the Charms are by your description.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;By my description?&quot;<br /> <br /> The book has been out for years now, have you still not actually read it? Was being unaware of the manuscript the basis of some of the arguments during the Kickstarter about what would and would not be a viable Lunar Charm?<br /> <br /> (They actually did have a Charm to shunt off damage to an acquired Heart's Blood shape in exchange for destroying it that was shown in an Attribute after we argued about that, by the way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}